    <page>
        <paragraphs>
            <title>General Form Quadratics</title>
            
            <p component="b" workspace="3in">
                So, we know how to graph quadratic equations if they are in the form <md>
                    f(x) = a(x-h)^2 + k
                </md>. But, what if it's not in this form?
                
            </p>
            <p component="a">
                So, we know how to graph quadratic equations if they are in the form <md>
                    f(x) = a(x-h)^2 + k
                </md>. But, what if it's not in this form? Then, we need to complete the square to make it that way.
                 
            </p>
        </paragraphs>
    </page>

    <page>
        <example workspace="4in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Use completing the square to write <md>
                        x^2 - 4x + 9
                    </md> in the form
                    <md>
                        a(x-h)^2 + k
                    </md>.
                    Then sketch the graph.
                </p>
            </statement>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>

    <page>
        <example workspace="4in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Use completing the square to write <md>
                        2x^2 + 5x - 10
                    </md> in the form
                    <md>
                        a(x-h)^2 + k
                    </md>.

                </p>
            </statement>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>

    <page>
        <example workspace="4in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Use completing the square to write <md>
                        3x^2 + 18x + 30
                    </md> in the form
                    <md>
                        a(x-h)^2 + k
                    </md>.
                    Then sketch the graph.
                </p>
            </statement>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>

    <page>
        <paragraphs>
            <title>Vertex of a Parabola</title>
            
<p component="b" workspace="4in">
    Now that we know how to convert between these forms, we can use that to help us analyze a quadratic function, potentially without changing the form.
</p>
<p component="a">
    Now that we know how to convert between these forms, we can use that to help us analyze a quadratic function, potentially without changing the form. Finding the vertex, know if max or min.
</p>

        </paragraphs>
    </page>

    <page>
        <example workspace="4in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Find the vertex of the parabola <md>
                        f(x) = 3x^2 - 7x + 13
                    </md>. Is this point a maximum or a minimum for the parabola?
                    
                </p>
            </statement>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>

    <page>
        <paragraphs>
            <title>Applications</title>
            
            <p component="b" workspace="4in">
                How can we use this for applications?
            </p>
            <p component="a">
                How can we use this for applications? If we have a word problem with a quadratic, we can now ask what the max or min value is.
            </p>
        </paragraphs>
    </page>

    <page>
        <example workspace="0in">
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    Assume that the average ticket price for a sporting event is given by 
                    <md>
                        p(t) = -\frac{5}{8}t^2 + \frac{35}{4}t + 100
                    </md>, where <m>p</m> is in dollars and <m>t</m> is the number of weeks after the start of the season. 
                    
                </p>
            </introduction>
            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Does the ticket price have a maximum or minimum value?
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        What is that value and where does it achieve it?
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>

    <page>
        <example workspace="4in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    A vegetable garden has been built alongside a solid wooden fence. This garden is built with <quantity><mag>16</mag><unit base="foot"/></quantity> of wire fencing on the three additional sides (excluding the wooden fence). What dimensions of the garden maximize its area?
                </p>
            </statement>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>
